<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Il Caffè</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1764–<a href="/years/1766">1766</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Il Caffè was a periodical produced in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> from June 1764 to May 1766 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pietro-verri">Pietro Verri</a>, his brother Alessandro and their circle, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-beccaria">Cesare Beccaria</a>. Modelled on English journals such as The Spectator, it discussed economics, law, science and literature in a lively style. It became a leading voice of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-enlightenment">Italian Enlightenment</a> and of reform in Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/il-caffe.jpg" alt="Il Caffè" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: it:Pietro Verri · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Il_caff%C3%A8_1764.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
